      "text": " 10%-2m, A is equal to 4.5cm2, which is equal to 4.5 into 10%-4m2, R is equal to 15o."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:07:36.556",
      "start": "00:07:25.645",
      "text": " Kappa is equal to 1xR into L by A, which is equal to 1 divided by 15o into 1.5 into 10%-2m2"
    },
    {
      "end": "00:07:46.099",
      "start": "00:07:36.556",
      "text": " m divided by 4.5 into 10 to the power minus 4m2, which is equal to 2.2 to 7 per meter."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:07:56.843",
      "start": "00:07:46.099",
      "text": " The electrical resistance of a column of 0.05 mole L inverse NaOL solution of length 50cm is"
    },
    {
      "end": "00:08:06.720",
      "start": "00:07:56.843",
      "text": " 5.55 into 10 cube ohm, calculate its resistivity. Area is equal to 0.785cm2."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:08:14.828",
      "start": "00:08:06.720",
      "text": " NaOL is equal to R into L divided by A, so R is equal to R into A divided by L."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:08:29.209",
      "start": "00:08:14.828",
      "text": " 5.55 into 10 cube ohm into 0.785cm2 divided by 50cm, which is equal to 87.135 ohm centimeter."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:08:34.447",
      "start": "00:08:29.209",
      "text": " So in this video, we will see the measurement of conductivity of ionic solution."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:08:38.218",
      "start": "00:08:34.447",
      "text": " How to know that an electrolytic solution can be seen as resistivity."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:08:42.188",
      "start": "00:08:38.218",
      "text": " How to calculate that resistivity, how to calculate conductivity."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:08:45.558",
      "start": "00:08:42.188",
      "text": " How to calculate that resistivity."
